 # MusicCat Architecture
 
-Stub - task 20 output goes here.
+## Overview
+MusicCat (Tonebox) is a music education management system built with FastAPI and SQLAlchemy. It provides comprehensive functionality for managing music lessons, instructors, students, studio rooms, and bookings.
+
+## System Architecture
+
+### Tech Stack
+- **Framework**: FastAPI (async)
+- **Database**: SQLAlchemy ORM with async support
+- **Data Validation**: Pydantic
+- **API Style**: RESTful with JSON responses
+
+### Directory Structure
+```
+/app
+├── core/                    # Core utilities (database, constants, schemas)
+├── lesson_schedule/         # Lesson scheduling and billing
+├── music_accounts/          # User authentication and profiles
+├── music_bookings/          # Booking management
+├── music_instruments/       # Instrument catalog and lessons
+├── music_lessons/           # Lesson management and rosters
+├── music_models/            # SQLAlchemy data models
+├── music_reports/           # Reporting and analytics
+├── music_rooms/             # Studio room management
+├── music_staff/             # Instructor and staff management
+├── practice_logs/           # Student practice tracking
+├── recital_hall/            # Recital event management
+└── tests/                   # Test suite
+```
+
+## Core Modules
+
+### 1. User & Account Management (`music_accounts/`)
+- User registration and authentication
+- Role-based access control (admin, staff, instructor, teacher, student)
+- User profile management
+
+### 2. Instructor Management (`music_staff/`)
+- Instructor profile creation and updates
+- Instructor schedule viewing
+- Instructor workload statistics
+
+### 3. Lesson Management (`music_lessons/`)
+- Lesson creation and scheduling
+- Lesson status updates
+- Lesson roster management
+
+### 4. Room Management (`music_rooms/`)
+- Studio room inventory
+- Room booking with conflict detection
+- Room availability checking
+
+### 5. Booking System (`music_bookings/`)
+- Unified booking model for lessons and rooms
+- Booking status management
+- Capacity validation for group lessons
+
+## Data Model Relationships
+
+### Core Entities
+- **User**: Base entity for all system users (students, instructors, staff)
+- **Instructor**: Extended profile for instructors (linked to User)
+- **Lesson**: Course definition with instructor and room assignments
+- **StudioRoom**: Physical classroom/studio space
+- **Booking**: Reservation record linking user to lesson or room
+- **Instrument**: Musical instrument definitions with teacher associations
+- **OldLesson**: Legacy lesson model (for backward compatibility)
+- **PracticeLog**: Student practice tracking
+- **Recital**: Special event management
+
+### Key Relationships
+- User ↔ Instructor (one-to-one optional)
+- Instructor ↔ Lesson (one-to-many)
+- Lesson ↔ StudioRoom (many-to-one)
+- Lesson ↔ Booking (one-to-many)
+- User ↔ Booking (one-to-many)
+- StudioRoom ↔ Booking (one-to-many)
+
+## API Design Principles
+- Async-first approach for better scalability
+- Role-based access control using dependencies
+- Pydantic models for request/response validation
+- RESTful resource naming conventions
+
+## Status
+- **Legacy Models**: OldLesson and related models exist for backward compatibility
+- **Dual Systems**: Two parallel lesson systems (OldLesson vs Lesson + Booking)
+- **Future Enhancement**: Conflict detection for instructors and students
