+## Overview
+This document describes the schedule conflict detection and resolution mechanisms in the Tonebox system.
+
+## Conflict Types
+
+### 1. Room Conflicts
+- **Definition**: Multiple bookings for the same studio room at overlapping time slots
+- **Detection Logic**: Time interval overlap check (start < end && end > start)
+- **Status Check**: Only considers bookings with status "pending" or "confirmed"
+- **Implementation**: `music_rooms/room_bookings.py:39-50` - `check_room_available()`
+
+### 2. Instructor Conflicts
+- **Definition**: An instructor assigned to multiple lessons at overlapping times
+- **Status**: Currently not implemented in the system (placeholder for future enhancement)
+- **Required Logic**: Check instructor availability when creating/updating lessons
+
+### 3. Student Conflicts
+- **Definition**: A student booked in multiple lessons at overlapping times
+- **Status**: Currently not implemented in the system (placeholder for future enhancement)
+- **Required Logic**: Check student's existing bookings when creating new bookings
+
+## Conflict Resolution Strategies
+
+### 1. Preventive Measures
+- Real-time availability check before booking creation
+- Capacity validation for group lessons (`music_bookings/booking_manager.py:43-55`)
+
+### 2. Resolution Options (Future)
+- Manual override by admin/staff
+- Automatic alternative time slot suggestions
+- Priority-based conflict resolution
+
+## Data Model Reference
+- `Booking`: Stores all reservations (rooms and lessons)
+- `StudioRoom`: Room definitions and status
+- `Lesson`: Course schedule and instructor assignments
+
+## API Endpoints
+- `POST /rooms/{room_id}/book`: Room booking with conflict check
+- `POST /bookings`: Generic booking with capacity check
